This is a lightly 'A'nnotated QBE.

I wanted to understand the internals of QBE a little better, but must have some
sort of learning disability that inhibits me being able to understand the terse
style that QBE is written in!

It's functionally unmodified, but adds some comments and renames some
functions/variables that made it easier for me to follow. YMMV, naturally.

It's not intended to be a fork, or aimed at upstreaming, it's more like an
"internals" document. I don't expect to continually rebase on master, but QBE
doesn't have high churn, so it shouldn't diverge too quickly, and shouldn't be
that hard to rebase if desired.


Original README follows:
------------------------


QBE - Backend Compiler              http://c9x.me/compile/

doc/    Documentation.
minic/  An example C frontend for QBE.
tools/  Miscellaneous tools (testing).
test/   Tests.
amd64/
arm64/
rv64/   Architecture-specific code.

The LICENSE file applies to all files distributed.

- Compilation and Installation

Invoke make in this directory to create the executable
file qbe.  Install using 'make install', the standard
DESTDIR and PREFIX environment variables are supported.
Alternatively, you may simply copy the qbe binary.
